{"title":"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6fa3bd14b7adda3243884b687b92e761f2cf1ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 4 + 12x + 6y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d801614503fbd91e19737cf363f5387d5b7155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = k + 4x + 12y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"182\" height=\"18\" /> intersect when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/f/a8f69200b2061bac4758de6e4511cc38e34a197c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\le k \\le b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />, and for no other values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/c/02c60c151331e235dc6d9df7ca403b6f0c9af39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7f2887e54c721dcb3ac59ead721a028b74400b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }68 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }104 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }140 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ }144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Both sets of points are quite obviously circles. To show this, we can rewrite each of them in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8b049b24412d943f2fd936428f3e388f2c8f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-x_0)^2 + (y-y_0)^2 = r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"203\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>The first curve becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/963be3e89ee170b585d4f844accbea3f9992fd63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-6)^2 + (y-3)^2 = 7^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"19\" />, which is a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/4/8144fc720051b8fbe49f359a72fec0072f0d044e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The second curve becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76aa7953c6bbbb0d9b0304ad21d2e7b5a4fbd978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-2)^2 + (y-6)^2 = 40+k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"19\" />, which is a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/8/dd87710da1743ebb0de8c0d280b13a036d422fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f818cbc45f19edee19dba23743f3ea1a0acced8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\sqrt{40+k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The distance between the two centers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and therefore the two circles intersect if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69f3fdcf4b363aace97d83f4750238d459e8e47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\leq r \\leq 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7bd4c04a776c649dea79c0c49c57633529ca9d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{40+k} \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"98\" height=\"19\" /> we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e15e03ab80aef4eff0bc7846507a5e93dbc74796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq -36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/998512a04094760c47118fc1ddf190f69cbb7506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{40+k}\\leq 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"19\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e3243e172f71d85c211c9e10b317e92852cea58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\leq 104$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7723cfdde363d7e84914cde55ba8620539d3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b-a = 104 - (-36) = \\boxed{140}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME\" title=\"1998 AHSME\">1998 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\